KNOWNBUG clang20
main.cpp
--cpp20
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
Concept-constrained specialization ordering with __is_pointer and
__remove_pointer builtins in requires clauses produces incorrect
results when CBMC uses Clang 20 as the preprocessor. The requires
clause requires(__is_pointer(T)) incorrectly matches non-pointer
types. The same test passes with Clang 18. The preprocessed C++
code is identical; the issue is in CBMC's internal state when
configured for Clang 20.
